The function is designed to find the maximum depth of nested parentheses within an individual group, with groups separated by spaces. The function counts the number of open parenthesis "(" encountered within an individual group and keeps track of the maximum count achieved which signifies the maximum depth. Once it has encounter a space " " or end of the input string, it notes down the maximum depth achieved in the result vector and resets the temporary depth and parenthesis count for the next group.

def find_word_start(s, start):
    while start < len(s) and s[start] == ' ':
        start += 1
    return start

def find_word_end(s, start):
    while start < len(s) and s[start] != ' ':
        start += 1
    return start

def reverse_range(s, start, end):
    while start < end:
        s[start], s[end] = s[end], s[start]
        start += 1
        end -= 1

def reverse_words_in_place(s, start, end):
    reverse_range(s, start, end)
    current_start = find_word_start(s, start)
    current_end = find_word_end(s, current_start)
    while current_start < end:
        reverse_range(s, current_start, current_end - 1)
        current_start = find_word_start(s, current_end)
        current_end = find_word_end(s, current_start)

